       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults under supervision. The 1,600 mg single dose is also double the usual maximum of 800 mg. At this dose, the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or 800 mg four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do intend 1,600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale for the order note. I'd still want to be sure before entering it."
